-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224/devtools-times/`.
+
+## WebAssembly image generator
+
+The homepage automatically renders a Julia fractal and offers a **Render a new image** button.
+The C renderer (`native/image-renderer.c`) runs entirely in a module Web Worker;
+only the completed RGBA buffer is transferred to the page for display on a canvas.
+The worker frees each native allocation after copying the result and is terminated
+when the component unmounts. Failed or timed-out renders offer a retry.
+
+The generated ES module and Wasm binary in `public/wasm/` are included so normal
+`npm run build` deployments do not require a C compiler. After changing the C source,
+install Emscripten (tested with 6.0.1), put `emcc` on PATH, and run:
+
+```sh
+npm run build:wasm
+npm run build
+```
+
+The build uses `-Oz -flto -g0`, ES module output, strict defaults, and growing memory.
+`ENVIRONMENT=web,worker` supports the dedicated browser worker without Node or shell
+runtime support. There is no dynamic linking or shared-memory/header requirement.
+
+For runtime diagnostics, run `npm run build:wasm:assertions` before building or
+starting the app. Check the browser console while the initial image and repeated
+renders complete, and expand **About these patterns** during rendering to verify
+responsiveness. Restore the release assets with `npm run build:wasm` afterward.
 
